From 1153adb69b7cf01a72f9563ade2bd7e26e9f2024 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 21:15:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/64] HIP/RDNA3: replay a captured decode graph as one PM4
 indirect buffer on an own ROCr queue (GGML_HIP_PM4)

A HIP graph costs ~2.75 us per kernel boundary on gfx1100: the CP's AQL front end
processes one packet per kernel (own AQL replay with any fence scope, kernarg in
VRAM or the barrier bit cleared: >= 2.08 us). The same chain as DISPATCH_DIRECT
packets in one PM4 IB, separated by CS_PARTIAL_FLUSH + ACQUIRE_MEM (GLK/GLV/GL1
invalidate), costs 0.46-0.86 us per boundary (microbenchmark, kernargs in VRAM).

After a graph is captured, its kernel nodes (one chain) are turned into a tape:
kernel descriptors from the HIP-loaded code objects (loader extension), explicit
kernargs from the node parameters at the offsets of the code-object metadata, the
hidden arguments as ROCclr fills them; kernargs in VRAM, IB in executable host
memory. The tape is submitted as one AMD vendor AQL packet (PM4_IB) with
system-scope acquire/release; ordering with the HIP stream on the host (stream
sync before, completion signal wait after, bounded). Same kernels and arguments:
bitwise identical. Graphs with other node types, several streams, scratch or
other implicit arguments keep cudaGraphLaunch. GGML_HIP_PM4=0 switches it off,
GGML_HIP_PM4_DEBUG=1 logs tape builds and fallbacks.

LFM2.5-24B-A2B Q5_K_M, KV q8_0, llama-bench tg128 -r 5, 3 rounds interleaved:
3.887 -> 3.424 ms/token (257.3 -> 292.1 t/s). Logit hashes a7ce25b73f887fed (d0),
b47452b9380b665b (d3000) unchanged; greedy md5 LFM 894e56e4..., Qwen plain
c4708318..., Qwen MTP 6f14e814... unchanged (Qwen tapes: 807-919 dispatches).
